          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "11.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " In Fig. 6.40, E is a point on side CB produced of an isosceles triangle ABC with AB = AC. If AD ⊥ BC and EF ⊥AC, prove that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm { A B D } \\sim \\Delta \\mathrm { E C F } ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.227,
            0.501,
            0.315
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "12.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Sides AB and BC and median AD of a triangle ABC are respectively proportional to sides PQ and QR and median PM of   PQR (see Fig. 6.41). Show that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta  ABC  \\sim \\Delta  PQR"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.578,
            0.151,
            0.762,
            0.27
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.578,
                0.151,
                0.762,
                0.27
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_24_image_5.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.633,
                0.279,
                0.731,
                0.298
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 6.40"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.321,
            0.5,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " D is a point on the side BC of a triangle ABC such that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle ADC = \\angle BAC"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Show that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "CA^{2}=CB.CD"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.379,
            0.501,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "14.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Sides AB and AC and median AD of a triangle ABC are respectively proportional to sides PQ and PR and median PM of another triangle PQR. Show that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm { A B C } \\sim \\Delta \\mathrm { P Q R }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.51,
            0.312,
            0.906,
            0.416
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.51,
                0.312,
                0.906,
                0.416
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_24_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.647,
                0.432,
                0.744,
                0.452
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 6.41"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.473,
            0.9,
            0.509
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "15.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A vertical pole of length 6 m casts a shadow 4 m long on the ground and at the same time a tower casts a shadow 28 m long. Find the height of the tower."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.513,
            0.9,
            0.577
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "16.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " If AD and PM are medians of triangles ABC and PQR, respectively where "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm { A B C } \\sim \\Delta \\mathrm { P Q R }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , prove that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{\\overline{AB}}{\\overline{PQ}} = \\frac{\\overline{AD}}{\\overline{PM}}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.603,
            0.252,
            0.622
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6.5 Summary"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.629,
            0.576,
            0.647
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In this chapter you have studied the following points :"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.649,
            0.9,
            0.684
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Two figures having the same shape but not necessarily the same size are called similar figures."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.687,
            0.718,
            0.705
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " All the congruent figures are similar but the converse is not true."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.708,
            0.9,
            0.744
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Two polygons of the same number of sides are similar, if (i) their corresponding angles are equal and (ii) their corresponding sides are in the same ratio (i.e., proportion)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.746,
            0.9,
            0.781
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " If a line is drawn parallel to one side of a triangle to intersect the other two sides in distinct points, then the other two sides are divided in the same ratio."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.784,
            0.9,
            0.818
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " If a line divides any two sides of a triangle in the same ratio, then the line is parallel to the third side."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.822,
            0.9,
            0.858
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " If in two triangles, corresponding angles are equal, then their corresponding sides are in the same ratio and hence the two triangles are similar (AAA similarity criterion)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.859,
            0.902,
            0.896
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " If in two triangles, two angles of one triangle are respectively equal to the two angles of the other triangle, then the two triangles are similar (AA similarity criterion)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.436,
            0.967,
            0.563,
            0.982
          ],
